This work-only actual Chrome campaign authenticated the complete frozen corrected188 Sketch stage before preparing a private host. The candidate client/layout/core/server were copied byte-identically. Current shared host/catalog/storage/shell files were captured exactly; the private host has one declared extra static route for `/apps/sketch/layout.mjs`. The route is an integration prerequisite: the current production host lacks it. No Studio source or old stage was changed.

Eight visible layout controls passed hand-derived exact fractional-coordinate expectations. Each passed one-step Undo and Redo. The generated group scene passed actual canvas-member selection (two members), Select all (three shapes), preserved member offsets, group-unit alignment, Undo and Redo. Both no-op history boundaries passed: already arranged and one selected group do not add Undo entries. A documented CUA/CDP real held mouse press plus canvas keyboard shortcut refused layout before mutation and released normally; no synthetic DOM events or product closure hooks were used.

An actual browser Save committed one scene; New scene emptied the canvas; page reload fetched a fresh disk-backed list; selecting the saved scene reopened the exact shape state. Actual native Export produced one successful HTTP document with matching scene positions and groups. The browser download-event bridge timed out after ten seconds, and the scoped debugger event observation was empty/truncated. Downloaded-file delivery/bytes remain unverified; no permission change or download-location search was attempted. Export HTTP/document acceptance is finite and distinct from file-download acceptance.

All inputs are generated fixtures. Browser observations read only DOM-backed scene JSON/status/selection/bounds/options. Actions used documented CUA locators, coordinate click, and scoped real input dispatch. Nine JPEG screenshots retain correct actual `.jpeg` filenames and source-scoped qualifications; interpret them with paired DOM/HTTP/disk records. No original GUI, original helper, native executable, timing, profiler or full suite executes in this campaign. Prior original3968 comparison results remain historical source-bound authority, not newly executed here.

The initial browser assertion used Node deepStrictEqual on equal arrays crossing result realms, causing a prototype-comparison failure after the first layout applied. Exact failed action body/message and partial observations remain retained. Serialized finite generated values/scenes were compared thereafter; the first layout was not repeated, and its Undo/Redo completed normally. Fixtures, candidate and expected coordinates did not change. A post-cleanup shell read requested an absent optional host.stderr file and returned exit1 with no error output; the host itself exited0 and normal cleanup/source checks passed. The absent error log is not a product failure.

Owned tab, host, relay and temporary data were closed/removed normally. User4311, existing hosts, other tabs, credentials, machine TLS/network protections and source epochs remain untouched. The owned browser tab alone was created and closed. The native download may have reached the browser's ordinary download directory, but the bridge returned no owned path; no file outside the owned temp/work directories was deleted or claimed verified. This finite browser campaign does not establish complete imported-element appearance, server/vendor/OS behavior, full product parity or comparative improvements.

The first source-only finalizer incorrectly required an `ok` property on the actual successful `{result: ...}` HTTP envelope. Its source and failed raw output remain unchanged. A separate v2 finalizer corrects that assertion and permits only an exact-byte reuse of the successful partial authority-after capture; both source substitutions and identities are recorded in `finalizer-correction.json`. The v2 finalizer passed without repeating browser actions or product/original execution. The validation's initial diagnostic list is retained as generated; this paragraph and `diagnostic-addendum.json` supplement it with the finalizer failure.

Root's later `work/sketch-layout-static-route-next` correction is a separate source epoch and is not the host used here. This campaign used the declared private statement insertion and preserved its inverse reconstruction. The later root staticMap insertion is not authenticated or accepted by this browser receipt. The inert browser body snapshot records the action and assertion sequence with the remaining controls grouped into two batches; it is not claimed to be a byte-exact transcript of every CUA cell.
